<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajgad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajgad is a hill fort in the Sahyadri range near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>. It was one of the key forts secured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> in building his power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a>. It served as his capital for many years before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raigad">Raigad</a>, and it was central to the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajgad.jpg" alt="Rajgad" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rohan sangodkar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suvela_machi,Rajgad_fort,_Maharashtra,India_July2015.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
